   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## wan-camera-control.json\n\nA clip with a camera you chose, not one the model invents\n\n**Does:** takes a **still** as the first frame and animates it along a **preset camera trajectory** - `Static`, `Pan Up/Down/Left/Right`, `Zoom In/Out`, `Anti Clockwise` / `ClockWise` (`WanCameraEmbedding`). The reason this flow exists: in the other Wan routes the camera is **text-driven and drifts** (E18's own finding), and here it is an input instead. Host: `wan2.1_fun_camera_v1.1_1.3B_bf16` (3.23 GB, **Apache-2.0**, official Comfy-Org repack) + the umt5 encoder, `clip_vision_h` and the Wan VAE we ship.\n**Measured (E18, 2026-10-10):** 81 frames per cell in **115 s** - about 1/20th of the VACE 14B route - with **identity holding** in all three cells tested (Static / Pan Left / Zoom In). The evidence sheet (`video/evidence/E18-camera-sheet.png`) shows exactly what each preset does: Static keeps the framing dead-still (drift gone), Pan Left walks the subject across frame, Zoom In goes full body -> chest close-up.\n**Knobs:** `camera_pose` (the preset) is the point of the flow; **width/height/length live on the `WanCameraEmbedding`, not on the target node** - the embedding *outputs* them and they are linked in, so its 512x512 in the upstream example silently overrides the node's own 832x480. It ships **512x512** because a portrait start image is *cropped* in 16:9 (measured: our own `char_heroine.png` loses her head at 832x480) - for 16:9, letterbox the start image first (`scripts/letterbox_16x9.py`, one command) and set the embedding's width/height to **832**/**480**. Also `steps`/`cfg` (20 / 6.0) and the **start image**: give it a clean, well-lit still - the first frame is the clip's first frame, so its composition is what the camera departs from.\n**Traps:** a portrait still into a landscape canvas crops - measured, the head goes first, which is what the letterbox step is for - and the subject is what must survive the pan), and the trajectory is a **fixed preset** - a bespoke camera path needs the node's JSON pose input, which this flow does not expose.\n**Siblings:** `wan-animate-motion.json` (S15) copies motion from a driving clip; `wan-vace-reference.json` (S28) writes motion from a prompt. This one is the cheap one.\n\n---\n*How to run it: story **S29** in `HOWTO.md`  \u00b7  Why it is this way: **E18** in the scenarios' `EXPERIMENTS` logs.*"
   ],
   "widgets_values_named": {
    "text": "## wan-camera-control.json\n\nA clip with a camera you chose, not one the model invents\n\n**Does:** takes a **still** as the first frame and animates it along a **preset camera trajectory** - `Static`, `Pan Up/Down/Left/Right`, `Zoom In/Out`, `Anti Clockwise` / `ClockWise` (`WanCameraEmbedding`). The reason this flow exists: in the other Wan routes the camera is **text-driven and drifts** (E18's own finding), and here it is an input instead. Host: `wan2.1_fun_camera_v1.1_1.3B_bf16` (3.23 GB, **Apache-2.0**, official Comfy-Org repack) + the umt5 encoder, `clip_vision_h` and the Wan VAE we ship.\n**Measured (E18, 2026-10-10):** 81 frames per cell in **115 s** - about 1/20th of the VACE 14B route - with **identity holding** in all three cells tested (Static / Pan Left / Zoom In). The evidence sheet (`video/evidence/E18-camera-sheet.png`) shows exactly what each preset does: Static keeps the framing dead-still (drift gone), Pan Left walks the subject across frame, Zoom In goes full body -> chest close-up.\n**Knobs:** `camera_pose` (the preset) is the point of the flow; **width/height/length live on the `WanCameraEmbedding`, not on the target node** - the embedding *outputs* them and they are linked in, so its 512x512 in the upstream example silently overrides the node's own 832x480. It ships **512x512** because a portrait start image is *cropped* in 16:9 (measured: our own `char_heroine.png` loses her head at 832x480) - for 16:9, letterbox the start image first (`scripts/letterbox_16x9.py`, one command) and set the embedding's width/height to **832**/**480**. Also `steps`/`cfg` (20 / 6.0) and the **start image**: give it a clean, well-lit still - the first frame is the clip's first frame, so its composition is what the camera departs from.\n**Traps:** a portrait still into a landscape canvas crops - measured, the head goes first, which is what the letterbox step is for - and the subject is what must survive the pan), and the trajectory is a **fixed preset** - a bespoke camera path needs the node's JSON pose input, which this flow does not expose.\n**Siblings:** `wan-animate-motion.json` (S15) copies motion from a driving clip; `wan-vace-reference.json` (S28) writes motion from a prompt. This one is the cheap one.\n\n---\n*How to run it: story **S29** in `HOWTO.md`  \u00b7  Why it is this way: **E18** in the scenarios' `EXPERIMENTS` logs.*"
   },
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
